---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import headshot from "../assets/headshot.jpeg";

const title = "Brandon Davenport";
const description =
	"Tech evangelist who ships. AI and data tooling at Hgraph, elected member of the Hiero Technical Steering Committee, and creator of the Hashgraph Enthusiasts Show.";

// Bump alongside any content edit to this page; feeds ProfilePage's dateModified.
const profileDateModified = "2026-08-02";
---

<BaseLayout
	title={title}
	description={description}
	profileDateModified={profileDateModified}
>
	<h1 class="visually-hidden">Brandon Davenport</h1>
	<section class="intro">
		<Image
			src={headshot}
			alt="Brandon Davenport"
			width={320}
			height={400}
			fit="cover"
			position="center"
			class="headshot"
		/>
		<p>
			I'm a tech evangelist who ships. For over ten years I've worked both
			sides: architecting systems with engineers, then getting on stage, on
			camera, and on the timeline to make people want in.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="prose">
		<p>
			These days I advise <a
				href="https://hgraph.com"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer">Hgraph</a
			> on AI product and go-to-market. Before that I built their AI and data tooling
			with the team: a{" "}
			<a
				href="https://docs.hgraph.com/mcp-server/setup-chatgpt"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>Model Context Protocol server and an AI data agent</a
			> that answer plain-English questions about Hedera Stats' ecosystem metrics.
			I'm an elected member of the{" "}
			<a href="https://hiero.org/tsc" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>Hiero Technical Steering Committee</a
			> under the Linux Foundation. And I <a href="/live-show"
				>stream live on X</a
			>, building in public.
		</p>
		<p>
			I got here by making things: brands, software, music, events. That's where
			the eye came from, and it still decides what's worth shipping, which
			matters more now that anyone can generate something that isn't. It's also
			why the standard I authored,{" "}
			<a
				href="https://hips.hedera.com/hip/hip-920"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer">HIP-920</a
			>, is about music metadata, and why before this I created and hosted the{
				" "
			}
			<a
				href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CpjLibi4jp4"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer">Hashgraph Enthusiasts Show</a
			> for three years and 146 episodes. I'm the one in the room with leaders: making
			introductions, running working groups, closing deals.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="cta">
		<p><a href="/live-show">Watch the live show</a></p>
		<p>
			<a href="mailto:hey@itsbrandond.com?subject=Add%20me%20to%20your%20list"
				>Get an email when I ship something</a
			>
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="cooking">
		<h2>Currently cooking</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Live streaming on X, talking about AI/crypto news and building.</li>
			<li>For hire consulting work (tell me what you're working on)</li>
			<li>A secret project that I can't talk about quite yet</li>
			<li>Advising Hgraph on product and marketing</li>
		</ul>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.intro {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: flex-start;
		gap: 1.5rem;
	}

	.intro p {
		flex: 1 1 16rem;
		margin: 0;
	}

	/* Fixed 4:5 box; fit/position on the <Image /> crop the square source to it. */
	.headshot {
		flex: 0 0 auto;
		width: 8rem;
		aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
	}

	.prose p {
		margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
	}

	.cta {
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
	}

	.cta p {
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
	}

	.cooking {
		margin-top: 3rem;
	}

	.cooking h2 {
		font-size: 1rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
	}

	.cooking ul {
		margin: 0;
		padding-left: 1.1rem;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.35rem;
	}
</style>
